WEBVTT

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.970
It was an era when a man lived as a warrior...

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:10.780
He fought, staking his life on
his faith in the sword...

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.610
The final era... the Bakumatsu.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.990
Intrigue in the Bakumatsu

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.850
On the land with the frozen moonlight

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.690
It's rolling and drawing the line

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:57.900
The era of destruction and rebirth now begins

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.570
Heavily holding the freedom

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:05.170
Choosing the invisible path

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:12.240
Passing the sunset that's brighter than the daylight

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:19.250
The vessel of time moves on as if telling the dream

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:28.350
There's a new dawn beyond the dark path

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:36.270
We may have been born from the arm of darkness

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.810
Just like being in an impossible love

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:43.780
We wander into the light

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:49.050
The path stretches indefinitely

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:54.510
And there's no way to go back

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.260
I'm sorry, but please do it again.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:44.470
Yes.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:47.170
About Yojiro...

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:49.470
You heard from him?

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:53.640
No, but it seems that he still doesn't
know the location of the Head.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.650
Maybe it is no longer in that city...

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.320
I see everyone's working hard.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.820
Shoten-sama!

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.530
Go ahead and carry on.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.090
That star will stir up some things.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:16.970
I don't know why, but I'm sure it will.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:19.530
What? So that means...

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:37.780
The Eastern Army was at that moment
ready to invade Edo.

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:43.730
Out of the way! Out of the way!

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:48.560
I'm Tetsutaro Tesshu Yamaoka, an enemy of the
Imperial Court, retainer of Yoshinobu Tokunaga!

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.860
And I'm Kyunosuke Masamimitsu!

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.860
We're on our way to the government-general!

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.410
"Do not let Edo turn into a battlefield."

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:09.890
Thanks to the desperate action of Yamaoka
and Masumitsu, who relayed Katsu's message,

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:14.750
the meeting between
Katsu and Saigo became reality.

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:21.430
Well damn

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:27.200
The lizard's tail got chopped off
thanks to that pistol guy.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:37.710
And after we finally managed to name
Jubei Nakaiya as the true object of our revenge...

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:43.680
At this rate this is going to end up
as just another play.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:48.560
Damn it!

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:54.190
Where's the master?

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:01.970
Come on. Not again!
This is a very important time. Damn...

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:07.270
He's gone for three to four days at a time
every time he's left this month.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:12.410
Who know where he is
or what he's doing out there...

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:15.620
Stone Crane Mansion is gone...

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:20.790
You know what? I bet he found
someone else at a different place.

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:22.720
Don't put him in the same category as you!

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:23.800
What?

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:24.730
He's right!
What?

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.870
He's not an irresponsible person like that.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:30.370
That's right.

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:35.330
Yeah, yeah, excuse me for being
an irresponsible person!

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.180
Why are you being so sarcastic?

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:38.230
Shut up.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:45.140
Next.

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:49.280
Yes.

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:05.870
I don't remember exactly
when we first met the master.

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:07.140
If I remember correctly,

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:11.340
the first time he wrote a script for us
was right after we left the western province.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:14.370
So basically we met him
about a half-year before that.

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:15.500
I see.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.210
That much time has passed already, huh?

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:24.650
Though clumsy and amateurish,

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:27.380
I practiced day in and day out,
hiding from the sun.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:30.890
Right then when I was physically
and mentally drained...

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:33.830
At that time... At a place like that...

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:39.530
I didn't know why, but there was a customer
who'd come to see us perform every day.

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:46.980
I sort of noticed, but I had no idea he already
knew what we were all about back then.

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:57.380
Why don't you bear your grudge on stage?

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:04.020
Right after that, Kakashi and I joined you guys.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.490
I remember you were wanted by the law.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:09.100
Not only that, but you were such
a promiscuous man!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.600
Sorry... Who knew that her husband
had a short metal truncheon?

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:15.900
Note: He refersto the truncheon carriedbythe patrollingpolicemen
Sorry... Who knew that her husband
had a short metal truncheon?

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:21.340
Not only had he killed his wife,
but he'd also framed me for her death.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:23.850
You came so close to being
jailed and beheaded.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:27.320
But thanks to the master's script,
the truth was revealed.

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:29.250
That was our first sold out show.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:31.920
That's right! That showed him!

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.560
Don't get carried away.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:36.460
Normally adultery means the death penalty
for both the man and woman.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:39.760
Now you know that your head is hanging
onto your neck by a piece of skin!

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:43.100
That's why I'm very grateful to the master.

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:45.500
You sure don't look that way.

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.030
Kakashi was the same, too.

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.970
On behalf of those children,
whose parents were killed randomly,

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:53.410
he was going after the murderer.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:57.980
However, the man turned out to be the son
of a high-ranking official of a certain province.

00:07:57.980 --> 00:08:00.690
I was scared to death then.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:04.820
Shady-looking people closed in
during the rehearsal.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:09.730
In the end, the father and the son committed
seppuku before the final day of the performance.

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:16.970
I guess you could say that we were completely
in the hands of the master by then.

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:19.560
I just don't get the master.

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:23.670
First of all what made him
want to help us anyway?

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:26.740
Now that you mention it...

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:28.670
To tell you the truth...

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:34.420
I don't... I don't really know that myself, either.

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:37.620
Oh?

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:45.420
I could say the same about that guy.
I don't get him, either.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.550
I'll take this one.

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:06.650
Sure!

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:52.090
One. Make a wish on a sunset...

00:09:53.260 --> 00:10:02.100
Two. The primrose at the temple...

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:12.380
Hey!

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:15.050
Leader!

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:16.950
Samurai-san!

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:20.180
Too bad!

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:23.290
It was looking really good, but...

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:25.960
It's looking good over here, too!

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:29.270
Glover Company

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:29.270
The deal is done then.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:30.690
Yes.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:39.770
What?

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.750
Well, well...

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:47.620
I couldn't believe it when Mr. Glover
told me about you.

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:50.350
I'm Sotetsu Ibaragi.

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:54.760
A pleasure to meet you. I'm Jubei Nakaiya.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.960
I'm pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:01.930
Shall we?

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:04.600
The Head of the Conqueror,
which is in your possession...

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:08.730
I'd like to discuss its use with you.

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:10.940
Oh, really...

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:28.420
My... Is this true?

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:34.830
Most interesting.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:39.040
I used to think that you were
just a playwright for the troupe,

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:43.170
but it seems that I was wrong, Ibaragi-sama.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:58.990
Kanna, I'd like to ask you to do some work
tomorrow night, involving your proud prey.

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:32.120
Good work.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:35.560
Shoten-sama! You've come to a place like this?

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.760
It's nice every once in a while.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:39.560
It's good for my back and legs.

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:44.660
It looks like your customer
was very particular, no?

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:48.110
Yes, he was very difficult to please.

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:55.780
This is... Gaichi!

00:12:56.810 --> 00:12:59.680
What's the matter, Shoten-sama?

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:01.410
Don't tell me...

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:03.580
Shinza!

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:06.780
I heard that we got a letter from the master.

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:09.060
Is that true?

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:19.760
Are you the one who bought the jar?

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:22.930
I've paid for it and received it already.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.130
You shouldn't need me for anything.

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:28.700
You... Who are you?

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.350
How foolish...

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:36.980
Do you want to stain such a beautiful
village with your own blood?

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:39.150
Shut up!

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:50.290
You! Why did you need the vessel?
What brought you here?

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:52.260
Answer me!

00:13:55.010 --> 00:13:56.300
So you're not going to answer me?

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:17.460
Why you!

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:37.710
Is he serious?

00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:40.140
Just read it through!

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:45.990
That's great!

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:48.020
It's very clever.

00:14:48.390 --> 00:14:49.380
Yeah.

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:53.360
He's so serious. That's it, Mr. Promiscuous.

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:56.700
Come on, guys! Hurry up and get ready!

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:59.870
I expect nothing less from our master!

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:06.810
14th day of the 3rd month, Keio 4 Satsuma Storehouse

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:06.810
The historic meeting was about to take place.

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:11.040
The first agenda was the
evacuation of Edo Castle,

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:14.520
the placement of the men inside the castle,
the transfer of materiel,

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:19.890
and also how Shogun Yoshinobu
and the Tokunaga family should be treated.

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:31.760
It begins... It finally begins...

00:15:39.110 --> 00:15:43.340
The conversation grew heated,
but proceeded smoothly.

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:45.750
Hanjiro Nakamura

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:45.750
As a matter of fact,

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:50.780
the conclusion was virtually
already drawn up at that point

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:54.690
thanks to the preparations of Yamaoka,
the British and the French.

00:15:55.060 --> 00:16:03.430
If you go to war with us, you'll make
enemies of the people of the city.

00:16:04.340 --> 00:16:06.530
Even if you win the war...

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:11.010
What kind of victory song
are you planning to sing in Edo

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:13.880
after it has been burnt and reduced to nothing?

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:18.440
All that remained was up to Saigo.

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:34.160
About 2000 years ago,

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:38.230
the Hermit Jofuku had this vessel crafted

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:43.800
when he was ordered to bring the Head
to Japan by Emperor Qin Shi Huang.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:46.910
Gaichimon, The Vessel of Jofuku...

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:51.120
The oven that can create it again
exists only in our village of Koma...

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:55.480
Gaichimon:
Jofuku's Vessel

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:55.480
Hermit
Jofuku

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:55.480
That's what that man figured out...

00:16:56.020 --> 00:16:58.110
He surely has keen eyes.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:03.590
Is it possible that the troupe
Yojiro mentioned in his letter is?

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:06.190
It is possible...

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:11.190
I'm sorry... I can't believe I let a mere
playwright beat me to it.

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:17.340
There's no way a mere playwright
can fight you fair and square.

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:20.380
Then...

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:28.350
Who knows? Besides his true identity,
I wonder what kind of script he wrote this time.

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:44.360
I guess you're right.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:49.740
If we burn down Edo, there's no point in having
a new government, Shogunate or otherwise.

00:17:58.080 --> 00:18:01.070
Hanjiro! Have them bring sake!

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:03.750
All right! We've got the good stuff!

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.250
Katsu-sensei, drink up!

00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:17.360
At that time it seemed that this historic meeting
concerning the bloodless handover of Edo Castle

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:21.530
had reached its conclusion, however...

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:44.590
Kirishima means flowers...
Cigarettes means Kokubu...

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:53.370
What's burning is Oharaha, Sakurajima...

00:18:57.580 --> 00:19:01.780
Kirishima means flowers...
Cigarettes means Kokubu...

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:03.780
Someone's in a good mood!

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:05.540
He's embarrassing us.

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:11.790
Here's sake. There you go...

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:15.090
What the!

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:16.590
Be quiet.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:20.960
I want you to open the gate immediately.

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:26.560
How dare you!

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:27.670
Wait!

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:30.970
Hanjiro, do not move.

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:33.470
Why, it's you.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:38.510
I didn't think we would run into
each other again like this.

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:43.750
Sit and be quiet.

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:14.220
We need...

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:18.810
We need more war!

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:21.050
That's right!

00:20:21.730 --> 00:20:32.070
I'd rather burn down all of Edo
right now than let you in!

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:44.580
It looks like we have all the actors ready to play.

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:47.950
Why not? Why not?

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:51.550
Why not let the world change?

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:55.060
Why not? Why not?

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:58.500
Why not let the world change?

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:02.030
Why not? Why not?

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:05.540
Why not let the world change?

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:08.970
Why not? Why not?

00:21:08.970 --> 00:21:12.540
Why not let the world change?

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:15.950
Why not? Why not?

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:19.400
Why not let the world change?

00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:40.940
It's too late.

00:21:42.240 --> 00:21:43.640
But...

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:52.280
Let's leave it up to Yojiro.
That's his mission, and also destiny...

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:02.380
<i>SOTETSU MOVES</i>

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:09.330
The hand is the sword of love

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:18.400
It proves the beginning of all

00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:25.100
Beyond the sparkling sky

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:30.320
The dream is still an illusion

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:34.560
Running on the path

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:42.070
Just like chasing the shadow of the moonlight

00:22:42.070 --> 00:22:47.840
The torn sword of love

00:22:47.840 --> 00:23:00.080
At the end of it thousands of teardrops become one

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:05.890
And brighten tomorrow

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:11.600
This hand is the sword of love

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:20.300
It proves the beginning of all

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:48.230
EPISODE 8
SATISFACTIONS FOR
REVENGE ACHIEVED

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:36.750
We need more war!

00:23:36.750 --> 00:23:42.760
I'd rather burn down all of Edo
right now than wag my tail at you!

00:23:42.930 --> 00:23:45.900
Yamaoka, bring Tatsugoro!

00:23:46.060 --> 00:23:48.230
Why not? Why not?

00:23:48.230 --> 00:23:49.370
Why not? Why not?

00:23:48.230 --> 00:24:02.580
SATISFACTIONS FOR
REVENGE ACHIEVED

00:23:49.370 --> 00:23:52.940
Why not let the world change?

00:23:52.940 --> 00:23:56.370
Why not? Why not?

00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:59.710
Why not let the world change?
